.rdata:10BD2E09                 db 'l orientation',0
.rdata:10BD2E17                 align 4
.rdata:10BD2E18 aControlsHowAut_2 db 'Controls how automatic recentering of the Horizontal axis is acco'
.rdata:10BD2E18                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C11D0+9o
.rdata:10BD2E59                 db 'mplished',0
.rdata:10BD2E62                 align 4
.rdata:10BD2E64 aObsoleteNoLong db 'Obsolete - no longer used',0
.rdata:10BD2E64                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1200+1Eo
.rdata:10BD2E7E                 align 10h
.rdata:10BD2E80 aMAngulardampin db 'm_AngularDamping',0 ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1240+Ao
.rdata:10BD2E91                 align 8
.rdata:10BD2E98 aHowMuchTimeItT_0 db 'How much time it takes for the aim to catch up to the target',27h
.rdata:10BD2E98                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1240+2Eo
.rdata:10BD2ED5                 db 's rotation',0
.rdata:10BD2EE0 aThePathToWhich db 'The path to which the camera will be constrained.  This must be n'
.rdata:10BD2EE0                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1290+9o
.rdata:10BD2F21                 db 'on-null.',0
.rdata:10BD2F2A                 align 10h
.rdata:10BD2F30 aThePositionAlo_0 db 'The position along the path at which the camera will be placed.  '
.rdata:10BD2F30                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C12C0+9o
.rdata:10BD2F71                 db 'This can be animated directly, or set automatically by the Auto-D'
.rdata:10BD2FB2                 db 'olly feature to get as close as possible to the Follow target.  T'
.rdata:10BD2FF3                 db 'he value is interpreted according to the Position Units setting.',0
.rdata:10BD3034                 align 8
.rdata:10BD3038 aHowToInterpret_0 db 'How to interpret Path Position.  If set to Path Units, values are'
.rdata:10BD3038                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C12F0+9o
.rdata:10BD3079                 db ' as follows: 0 represents the first waypoint on the path, 1 is th'
.rdata:10BD30BA                 db 'e second, and so on.  Values in-between are points on the path in'
.rdata:10BD30FB                 db ' between the waypoints.  If set to Distance, then Path Position r'
.rdata:10BD313C                 db 'epresents distance along the path.',0
.rdata:10BD315F                 align 10h
.rdata:10BD3160 aWhereToPutTheC db 'Where to put the camera relative to the path position.  X is perp'
.rdata:10BD3160                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1320+9o
.rdata:10BD31A1                 db 'endicular to the path, Y is up, and Z is parallel to the path.  T'
.rdata:10BD31E2                 db 'his allows the camera to be offset from the path itself (as if on'
.rdata:10BD3223                 db ' a tripod, for example).',0
.rdata:10BD323C                 align 10h
.rdata:10BD3240 aHowAggressivel_5 db 'How aggressively the camera tries to maintain its position in a d'
.rdata:10BD3240                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1350+Ao
.rdata:10BD3281                 db 'irection perpendicular to the path.  Small numbers are more respo'
.rdata:10BD32C2                 db 'nsive, rapidly translating the camera to keep the target',27h,'s '
.rdata:10BD32FD                 db 'x-axis offset.  Larger numbers give a more heavy slowly respondin'
.rdata:10BD333E                 db 'g camera. Using different settings per axis can yield a wide rang'
.rdata:10BD337F                 db 'e of camera behaviors.',0
.rdata:10BD3396                 align 4
.rdata:10BD3398 aHowAggressivel_6 db 'How aggressively the camera tries to maintain its position in the'
.rdata:10BD3398                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C13A0+Ao
.rdata:10BD33D9                 db ' path-local up direction.  Small numbers are more responsive, rap'
.rdata:10BD341A                 db 'idly translating the camera to keep the target',27h,'s y-axis off'
.rdata:10BD3455                 db 'set.  Larger numbers give a more heavy slowly responding camera. '
.rdata:10BD3496                 db 'Using different settings per axis can yield a wide range of camer'
.rdata:10BD34D7                 db 'a behaviors.',0
.rdata:10BD34E4                 align 8
.rdata:10BD34E8 aHowAggressivel_7 db 'How aggressively the camera tries to maintain its position in a d'
.rdata:10BD34E8                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C13F0+Ao
.rdata:10BD3529                 db 'irection parallel to the path.  Small numbers are more responsive'
.rdata:10BD356A                 db ', rapidly translating the camera to keep the target',27h,'s z-axi'
.rdata:10BD35A5                 db 's offset.  Larger numbers give a more heavy slowly responding cam'
.rdata:10BD35E6                 db 'era. Using different settings per axis can yield a wide range of '
.rdata:10BD3627                 db 'camera behaviors.',0
.rdata:10BD3639                 align 10h
.rdata:10BD3640 aHowToSetTheVir db 'How to set the virtual camera',27h,'s Up vector.  This will affec'
.rdata:10BD3640                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1440+9o
.rdata:10BD367B                 db 't the screen composition, because the camera Aim behaviours will '
.rdata:10BD36BC                 db 'always try to respect the Up direction.',0
.rdata:10BD36E4                 align 8
.rdata:10BD36E8 aHowAggressivel_8 db 'How aggressively the camera tries to track the target rotation',27h
.rdata:10BD36E8                                         ; DATA XREF: sub_100C1470+Ao
.rdata:10BD3727                 db 's X angle.  Small numbers are more responsive.  Larger numbers gi'
